A column renamed is, to SQLite's listings, one column gone and another
new: refused, since the old one's values would go. There is no rename;
drop the old one on purpose (its values go), or keep it beside the new.

== before
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, title TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
INSERT INTO dish VALUES (1, 'soup');

== after
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '') STRICT;

== error
column `dish.title` is in the database, not in schema.sql: its values would go. Keep it, or drop it on purpose: `-- @drop 1 column dish title` in schema.sql (with `-- @release 1`). Renamed? Drop it, and fill the new one from it: `-- @from 1 column dish <new> = "title"`.
